# Face Detection

A small Python and OpenCV application that uses a webcam to detect faces in real time.

When a face is detected, the application draws a bounding box around it and displays a label below the detected area.

## How It Works

The application captures video from the webcam and processes each frame:

```text
Webcam
  ↓
Frame
  ↓
Grayscale
  ↓
Haar Cascade
  ↓
Face Detection
  ↓
Bounding Box + Label
```

Face detection is handled using a pre-trained Haar Cascade provided by OpenCV.

## Installation

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/Minuanoooo/face_detection.git
cd face_detection
```

Create a virtual environment:

```bash
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
```

Install the dependencies:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## Usage

Run the application:

```bash
python main.py
```

A window with the webcam feed will open.

Press `q` to exit the application.

## Requirements

* Python 3
* OpenCV 4.x
* A working webcam

## Project Structure

```text
face_detection/
├── main.py
